  "preserve_wire_responses": true,
  "purpose": "Cell ROLL-AA (board route F2, docs/handoff/2026-09-24-fable51/HANDOFF-STAGE3-FOR-CHATGPT-v1.md section 7.3): the WITHIN-FLIGHT A/A null of the Stage-3 variant-rollout methodology. Cell ROLL-1's grouped-Solver fragment with EXACTLY the Solver group changed to the E2b greedy-repeat twin form at N = 2 -- the locked v2.0 plan's Solver answering the IDENTICAL prompt twice for each row, greedy -- flown on the first 200 rows of the R01C construction roster. The two samples of one Solver visit are two contacts of the SAME request (reproduction.ojw.native_group_solver): same messages, same speech packet, same supplied knowledge, same response format; the ONLY field that differs between them is the composed decoding seed (reproduction.ojw.native_request.compose_solver_sample_decoding_params: seed = fragment_seed + seed_offset + sample_index), which llama.cpp's greedy path does not consult. Whatever paired per-row difference the read then measures is the measurement floor itself -- batch-composition nondeterminism and nothing else -- and that number becomes h_within, the margin every ROLL-2 variant comparison at n = 200 is read against. DESCRIPTIVE: no admission verdict, no comparator, no gate.",
  "service_session": "serving-slurp-native-candidate-five-train-a-np4-v1",
  "split_id": "STAGE3-CONSTRUCTION-R01C",
  "stage3_algorithm": {
    "id": "shared-rollout",
    "note": "ROLL-AA exercises the SAME algorithm-neutral rollout substrate cell ROLL-1 registered -- the grouped Solver, its custody and its commit -- and applies no learned context of its own. It is the A/A NULL of that substrate: two greedy repeats of one prompt, so the paired per-row difference it measures is the methodology's own measurement floor rather than any operator's effect. Declared 'shared-rollout' for exactly that reason; it is not a family arm and carries no credit_assignment or update operator.",
    "operators_used": [
      "rollout"
    ]
  }
